# Location: ./CITATION.cff
# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0). GitHub renders this as a
# "Cite this repository" button; tools such as Zotero and cffconvert read it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DockVerseHub or its benchmark harness in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DockVerseHub: A Reproducible Docker Learning and Benchmarking Platform"
abstract: >-
  DockVerseHub is a structured, hands-on Docker curriculum (13 concept modules,
  8 runnable labs) combined with a dependency-free research harness for
  controlled, statistically reported container experiments covering image
  footprint, build caching, multi-stage builds and cold-start latency.
authors:
  - family-names: Praveen
    given-names: Satvik
    email: satvikpraveen707@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/DockVerseHub"
url: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/DockVerseHub"
license: MIT
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
keywords:
  - docker
  - containers
  - reproducible research
  - benchmarking
  - devops
  - education
  - buildkit
  - kubernetes
